# Forgets a session. It deletes the session, the people met in it with their
# faces and appearances, every appearance recorded in it, and its
# conversations (walkie-database ADR-0010). People kept across sessions stay.
# This cannot be undone.

# The session to forget, session.id. 0 means the open session. The id may
# name a session that has ended.
int64 session_id
---
# False when the database failed. message then starts with "The database
# could not" and says why. Forgetting a session that is not there succeeds
# and forgets nothing. Session ids are never given twice, so a retry with the
# same session_id after a lost answer is safe. A retry with 0 forgets
# whichever session is open by then.
bool success
# For example "Forgot session 4 and its 2 people." or "No session is open,
# so nothing was forgotten."
string message
# The session that was forgotten. 0 when there was none.
int64 session_id
# How many people were forgotten with it.
uint32 people
